---
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
import {CONTACT} from '../consts';
// Written from what BeerMat actually stores (docs/ONLINE.md, docs/ARCHITECTURE.md); worth having reviewed.
const updated = '28 October 2026';
---
<Page title="Privacy policy · BeerMat" description="What BeerMat keeps about you, why, and how to get it or delete it.">
	<article class="wrap prose max-w-3xl py-10">
		<p class="eyebrow">Last updated {updated}</p>
		<h1 class="text-4xl">Privacy policy</h1>
		<p>This explains what BeerMat keeps about you and why. BeerMat is run by <strong>Daniel Weatherall, trading as BeerMat, Flat Above, 5 Albert Street, Derby DE1 2DS</strong> (“we”), the data controller for BeerMat Online. Questions or requests: <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT}`}>{CONTACT}</a>.</p>

		<h2>Playing a quiz</h2>
		<p>You can play any BeerMat quiz without an account. Your team name, answers, scores and any team photo are kept on the quizmaster’s laptop for that quiz, not by us. The venue or quizmaster running the quiz is responsible for that information; ask them about it.</p>

		<h2>A BeerMat Online account (optional)</h2>
		<p>If you make an account in the BeerMat app or on the quiz desk, we keep:</p>
		<ul>
			<li>your email address, the name you choose to show, and your password (stored only as a one-way hash);</li>
			<li>your usual team name and profile picture, if you add them, and your privacy choices;</li>
			<li>the quiz results you choose to save (event, team, position, points and the venue’s laptop that signed them);</li>
			<li>the venues you save as favourites.</li>
		</ul>
		<p>We use these to run your profile, statistics and badges, and, only if you switch it on, to show your name (and picture, if you allow it) on public leaderboards. The lawful basis is our contract with you to provide the service you signed up for.</p>

		<h2>Venues and quizmasters</h2>
		<p>For a venue’s page we keep its public details (name, address, website, location and quiz nights), the account of the person who runs it, and the quiz laptops registered to it. While a quiz laptop is signed in to an account, we keep its computer name, the quiz’s title and the addresses where that account’s other devices (another desk, a TV, a phone) can reach it, until it signs out or a day after it was last heard from; for a TV signed in to an account, its name and when it was last used. A venue can choose to share each quiz’s team names, positions and points with us. Venue plans, their dates and the venue’s Stripe customer reference are kept for billing. For the shared buzzer library we keep each clip a venue shares, with which venue and laptop shared it (never shown to other venues), and reports about clips.</p>

		<h2>Counting quizzes</h2>
		<p>When a live quiz finishes, the quizmaster’s laptop sends us a random number that stands for “one quiz finished”, so the website can show how many quizzes BeerMat has run. Nothing else goes with it: no venue, team, answer or score. A venue can switch this off on the quiz desk (Settings → Quiz room → Count this venue’s quizzes).</p>

		<h2>Finding quizzes and reports</h2>
		<p>If you use “near me”, your phone sends a rounded position for that search only; we don’t store it. If you report a problem with a venue page, we keep what you wrote and, if you were signed in, your account.</p>

		<h2>Who else handles it</h2>
		<ul>
			<li><strong>Oracle Cloud</strong> hosts BeerMat Online, in London.</li>
			<li><strong>Cloudflare</strong> runs this website, the downloads and our domain’s DNS.</li>
			<li><strong>Resend</strong> sends account emails (confirming your address, resetting your password).</li>
			<li><strong>Stripe</strong> handles payments for BeerMat Pro; we never see card details.</li>
		</ul>
		<p>We don’t sell your information or use it for advertising. There are no advertising or tracking cookies.</p>

		<h2>How long we keep it</h2>
		<p>Your account and saved results stay until you delete them. Deleting your account (in the app: Profile → <em>Delete my account and results</em>) removes it and everything kept with it straight away; copies in our backups are gone within 30 days. Billing records are kept as long as the law requires.</p>

		<h2>Your rights</h2>
		<p>You can download everything we keep about you (Profile → <em>Download everything BeerMat Online holds about you</em>), correct it, or delete it at any time in the app. You can also ask us by email to access, correct, delete or restrict your information, or object to how we use it. If you’re unhappy with how we handle it, you can complain to the Information Commissioner’s Office (<a href="https://ico.org.uk">ico.org.uk</a>).</p>
	</article>
</Page>
